1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Project Options

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:11,000
In this tutorial, we'll explain project options in Burp Suite

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,000
and how you can save and load your favourite project options.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Project options include everything within the Project Options tab

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:28,000
at the top of Burp, and also everything within individual tools in their Options tab.

6
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:34,000
If you use an on-disk project, these options are automatically saved within the project data.

7
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:40,000
So any changes that you make are maintained when you reopen an existing project.

8
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:47,000
But you can also save project options to a configuration file so that you can use these again.

9
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:55,000
One way to do this is through the Project menu, go to Project Options, and Save Project Options.

10
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:02,000
So if I just give this a name, we've saved them.

11
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:10,000
You can also do this from individual configuration panels if you click the Save Options item from the gear icon.

12
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:14,000
This will just save the options for that single panel.

13
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:29,000
So if we restart Burp, when Burp reopens, we can select to use the configuration file that we saved.

14
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:36,000
This means that the new project will get created using those options that I saved to disk.

15
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:48,000
We can also load project options at any time through the Project menu, or within individual panels.

16
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:53,000
We can do the same thing through the gear icon and choose Load Options.

17
00:01:53,000 --> 00:02:02,000
If you wish, you can configure Burp to always load your preferred config file by default for new projects.

18
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:12,000
So to do this, in the Startup Wizard, if you select your preferred config file and check this box that says Default to the above in future,

19
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:21,000
when you start and open a new project, Burp will select the same configuration file by default without you having to choose it.

20
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:29,000
So that's how project options work in Burp Suites, and how you can save and load your favorite options.

21
